PROJECT TITLE: 
LvlUP

PROBLEM STAEMENT:

   The Philippine Science High School System (PSHS System) implements a six-year STEM-based curriculum designed to develop students' scientific 
and technological capabilities, critical thinking, and other essential skills (Philippine Science High School System, n.d.). Within this 
academic setting, students may have different learning difficulties, study habits, and preferences for reviewing lessons. To examine these
experiences among the students of PSHS-EVC, a survey was conducted to identify challenging subjects, factors affecting studying, 
preferred learning methods, and interest in game-based learning. In the survey, 16 out of 21 respondents (76.1%) reported that they sometimes or
often struggle in undrestanding their lessons, indicating a learning need that our proposed platform could explore addressing. In response, this project proposes LvlUP, an experimental 
supplementary learning platform that incorporates interactive quizzes, game-based challenges, rewards, and progress tracking to make lesson review 
more engaging. The platform will be evaluated through user testing to assess its functionality, usability, and perceived usefulness as a 
supplementary learning tool.

PROJECT OBJECTIVES:

  General Objective

To develop the study habits of the student of PSHS - EVC with the use of a gamified educational platform. In which this platform 
supports lesson reviewing through entertaining interactive activities. This application also serves as a guide for the junior high students 
into finding an efficient study habit as they venture through a unique curriculum.

  Specific Objectives

1. To identify the learning difficulties, study preferences, and preferred game-based features of students through a survey before finalizing the platform's design.
2. To develop a functional educational platform with interactive quizzes, points, badges, and progress tracking before the end of the project development period.
3. To provide educational activities that allow students to review selected lessons and receive immediate feedback on their quiz answers.
4. To evaluate the platform's usability, functionality, and perceived engagement through testing with approximately 1-10% of the intended student users after development.
5. To use feedback and test results to identify areas for improvement before finalizing the platform.

PLANNED FEATURES:

- File Upload: Upload PDFs, pictures, or plain text as study sources.
- Interactive Quizzes: Provides questions related to selected lessons, with immediate feedback on answers.
- Points and Rewards: Awards points for completing learning activities and badges for reaching defined milestones.
- Progress Tracking: Displays quiz scores, completed activities, and learning progress.
- Levels and Challenges: Organizes activities into levels or challenges to encourage continued participation.
- Learning Materials: Provides access to selected educational content for review.
- User-Friendly Interface: Offers simple navigation so students can
  easily access learning activities.
- Performance Summary: Shows users their results and areas they may need to review further.
- AI-Assisted Learning: Integrates an existing AI model through an API to generate explanations and practice questions based on study materials submitted by users.
- AI-Generated Explanations and Practice Questions: Provides simplified explanations, hints, and additional practice questions based on the submitted study materials. 
  The relevance and accuracy of the generated responses may vary.

PLANNED INPUTS AND OUTPUTS:
->INPUTS:
• PDF File/s         
